From: Canonical patch progression <213740+schancel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:24:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fixup! rpc: drain independent submissions through a
 bounded commit owner

Use callback-based admission completion and Asio awaitables, retain synchronous callers and direct overload fallback, fence primary and built-in secondary notification queues without blocking RPC workers. Completion posts to the originating executor/strand, owns payloads through delivery, and safely ignores late retained callbacks after initiation exceptions. Preserve sequential JSON arrays and callback/relay ordering. Shared combined gate146cases PASS; benchmark pending.
